    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass (2/2, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule so that `POST /api/owners` defaults `registrationDate` to the server's current date when none is supplied, keeps a supplied date, and returns it in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional, not required). Because DTOs are generated from this spec, `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` now carry a `LocalDate registrationDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`, column `registration_date`) field with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import. MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions (no mapper edits needed).\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the payload omits it (following the existing telephone/email normalization pattern); supplied dates pass through unchanged.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres for consistency). Existing seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they\u2019re unaffected.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (retains `2020-06-15`).",
